# ==========================================================================
# Managed by CanonSync — canonical LICENSE template (whole mode)
# Source of truth: canon/LICENSE · Do not hand-edit inside a synced repo.
# ==========================================================================

LICENSE — PLACEHOLDER

This file is a canonical LICENSE template synced by CanonSync in "whole"
mode, meaning it REPLACES the entire LICENSE file in each target repo.

It is disabled by default in canonsync.config.json ("enabled": false) so
that CanonSync never overwrites a repo's license until you deliberately turn
it on. Before enabling it:

  1. Replace this entire file with your actual license text.
  2. Confirm the same terms are correct for every repo you sync to — whole
     mode makes no per-repo exceptions.
  3. Set "enabled": true for the "license" item in canonsync.config.json.

Authoritative licensing terms and governance for this ecosystem are
maintained separately. Refer to your governance/licensing repository for
the definitive terms before publishing this file.

# ==========================================================================
# Notes on why this file is NOT expanded like gitignore/gitattributes/
# editorconfig masters
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Those three are technical config templates: adding more community-standard
# patterns is objectively safe, since an unused rule for an OS/editor/
# language you don't touch is simply inert.
#
# A LICENSE is a legally operative document. There is no generic "more
# complete" version to expand this into without either:
#   (a) fabricating legal terms that don't reflect your actual ecosystem's
#       licensing model, or
#   (b) defaulting to a standard OSI license (MIT/Apache-2.0/GPL/etc.) that
#       may not match the subscription / official-use / governed-participation
#       structure a project is actually built around.
#
# Either of those risks silently shipping incorrect legal terms across every
# repo CanonSync touches in whole mode. So this stays a placeholder here.
# ==========================================================================
